  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song-dance repertoire of the Tharu of Nepal's western and central Terai, among them Dang, Bardiya, Kailali and Chitwan. Sakhiya is danced by women in a circle from Krishna Janmashtami through Dashain and Tihar while men play the madal; maghauta is danced at Maghi, the Tharu new year; and jhumra is a western Tharu song-dance sung at Dashain and other festive occasions. Radio Nepal and Music Nepal have carried Tharu-language songs.",
